[
  {
    "label": "961ffd7b-3ddc-5e8e-8154-c1d2c7260e33",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186105733,
        "id": "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea",
        "title": "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "961ffd7b-3ddc-5e8e-8154-c1d2c7260e33",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,-2,-3)$, $B(-1,-2,-1)$, $C(-2,-4,-2).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i-2j-k)-(-2i-2j-3k) \\\\  & =i+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-4j-2k)-(-2i-2j-3k) \\\\  & =-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =4i-j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-1,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "1fe13558-c04f-55d0-9b8b-2599812b93b7",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
