  {
    "label": "f8041b05-a284-546b-8ef4-48d196f31e3d",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186105733,
        "id": "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea",
        "title": "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "f8041b05-a284-546b-8ef4-48d196f31e3d",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-3,-3,-4)$, $B(-6,1,-6)$, $C(-5,-2,-10).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-6i+j-6k)-(-3i-3j-4k) \\\\  & =-3i+4j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-5i-2j-10k)-(-3i-3j-4k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot (-6)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-((-3)\\cdot (-6)-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+((-3)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-22i-14j+5k \\\\  & =⟨-22,-14,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-22)^{2}+(-14)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{705}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{705}}{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "0996cec4-943d-5dc2-aad8-fb7a8fd031b4",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
