        "title": "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "c090616c-dc00-5125-b106-d8e2aee23a6a",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(2,0,1)$, $B(3,-1,-2)$, $C(-1,-2,-6).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i-j-2k)-(2i+k) \\\\  & =i-j-3k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i-2j-6k)-(2i+k) \\\\  & =-3i-2j-7k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-2,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-7)-(-3)\\cdot (-2))i-(1\\cdot (-7)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))k \\\\  & =i+16j-5k \\\\  & =⟨1,16,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{16}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{282}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{282}}{2}.\n$$",
